@translation labeled en project

@(1 = 1-3) Say to @wPN{@wDN{Nanna}-ki-aŋ}, the general: this is what @wRN{Lipit-@wDN{Eštar}}, your lord, says:

@(4 = 4-7) Because of  @varh[t3204.v1]{enemy troops } @vart[t3204.v2,t3204.v1]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} the enemy },  @varh[t3204.v3]{I, the king, have sent you a letter } @vart[t3204.v4,t3204.v3]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} I have sent a letter }. @wPN{Atta-mannum}, who pleases his lord, is (?) a better  @varh[t3204.v5]{servant to his lord } @vart[t3204.v6,t3204.v5]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} man } than you! Why is it that  @varh[t3204.v7]{you have not been avenging your lord, and not keeping me informed } @vart[t3204.v8,t3204.v7]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} while I (?) have kept the soldiers loyal (?), you have not stationed them among those people }?  @vart[t3204.v9,t3204.v9]{@varn{1 ms. adds:} So now you are to station the troops there. }

#etcsl#altGrpo
#etcsl#alt t3204.v1 t3204.v2
#etcsl#alt t3204.v3 t3204.v4
#etcsl#alt t3204.v5 t3204.v6
#etcsl#alt t3204.v7 t3204.v8
#etcsl#altGrpc

@(8 = 8-10) Now,  @varh[t3204.v10]{I have sent to you in haste } @vart[t3204.v11,t3204.v10]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} they have pursued (?) }  @varh[t3204.v12]{2000 } @vart[t3204.v13,t3204.v12]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} 4000 } @vart[t3204.v14,t3204.v12]{@varn{1 other ms. has instead:} 3000 } soldiers  @varh[t3204.v15]{who are spear-throwers } @vart[t3204.v16,t3204.v15]{@varn{ 1 ms. has instead:} who are …… spear-throwers },  @varh[t3204.v17]{2000 } @vart[t3204.v18,t3204.v17]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} 4000 } soldiers  @varh[t3204.v19]{who are archers } @vart[t3204.v20,t3204.v19]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} who are …… archers }, and  @varh[t3204.v21]{2000 } @vart[t3204.v22,t3204.v21]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} 1000 } soldiers  @varh[t3204.v23]{who are double-axe wielders } @vart[t3204.v24,t3204.v23]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} who are …… double-axe wielders }.

#etcsl#altGrpo
#etcsl#alt t3204.v10 t3204.v11
#etcsl#alt t3204.v12 t3204.v13 t3204.v14
#etcsl#alt t3204.v15 t3204.v16
#etcsl#alt t3204.v17 t3204.v18
#etcsl#alt t3204.v19 t3204.v20
#etcsl#alt t3204.v21 t3204.v22
#etcsl#alt t3204.v23 t3204.v24
#etcsl#altGrpc

@(11 = 11-17) The enemy has camped down in @wSN{Iri-gibil}. Chase them away from those settlements; do not ……. Guard (?) each city ……. Do not let these cities out of your grasp. Station your people -- it is urgent!
